# Disk layout of the FRDM-IMX95-PRO image (provisional, SPEC row ftpm, #140).
# Source: meta-freescale files/wic/imx-imx-boot-bootpart.wks.in (the BSP's own
# layout), minus its raw imx-boot entry. The boot container is written to its
# own raw offset by the boot-container flow, with the M7 image, so imx-boot (and
# the Freescale EULA it brings) stays out of this image.
# The root file system stays read-only; /data is a separate writable partition,
# the home of the fTPM NV (OP-TEE REE-FS storage), mounted before tee-supplicant
# starts (recipes-security/optee/trusted-imx95-tee-nv). SPEC row 34 (ftpm): the
# NV is wiped with the root file system, so tee-data is recreated empty by every
# full-image flash and is formatted with the root file system (docs/ftpm/README.md).
# Boot partition: the BSP's line (bootimg-partition holds the kernel, DTBs and
# boot files from IMAGE_BOOT_FILES); 256 MiB as in the BSP.
part /boot --source bootimg-partition --ondisk mmcblk --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 8192 --fixed-size 256
# Root: the BSP's line, with a fixed 1024 MiB. MISSING: no survey sizes the root; provisional.
# The file system fills the partition (wic makes it as large as --fixed-size); nothing is reserved.
# tee-nv-wipe keeps the root binding token in the first sector of the partition, the boot-sector
# padding in front of the ext4 superblock, which any write of the file-system image replaces
# (docs/ftpm/README.md). That needs 4096-byte blocks, so block 0 holds the superblock too and
# a sparse copy cannot skip it; --mkfs-extraopts pins the block size (wic's mkfs.ext4 call).
# Not built here: that wic passes the option on is unverified; the unit fails closed if it does not.
part / --source rootfs --ondisk mmcblk --fstype=ext4 --label root --part-name root --align 8192 --fixed-size 1024M --mkfs-extraopts "-b 4096"
# tee-data, after the root partition. MISSING: no survey sizes it; 64 MiB is provisional.
part /data --ondisk mmcblk --fstype=ext4 --label tee-data --part-name tee-data --no-fstab-update --fixed-size 64M

# The BSP takes the table type from IMX_BOOTLOADER_PTABLE; GPT is kept here for the partition names
# (the kernel's PARTNAME, which tee-data-mount reads on the root's own disk).
bootloader --ptable gpt
